  "question": {
    "text": "If the filament of a <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>100</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">W</mi></math>&nbsp;bulb has an area <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>25</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><msup><mi>cm</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math>&nbsp;and behaves as a perfect black body, find the wavelength corresponding to the maximum in its energy distribution. [Given&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>σ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>5.67</mn><mo>×</mo><mn>1</mn><msup><mn>0</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>8</mn></mrow></msup><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">J</mi><mo>&nbsp;</mo><msup><mtext>m</mtext><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mtext>&nbsp;</mtext><mo>s</mo><mo>&nbsp;</mo><msup><mtext>K</mtext><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></msup></math>,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>b</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>89</mn><mo>×</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi></math>]"
  },
